@page "/privacy"
@model PrivacyModel

<header class="banner">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › Privacy policy</p>
    <h1 class="d2">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
        How we collect, use and protect personal information, in line with the Protection of Personal
        Information Act, 2013 (POPIA). Last reviewed @PolicyReview.Describe(PolicyReview.Privacy).
    </p>
</header>

<section class="band band--white">
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:74ch">
        <h2 class="d4">Who we are</h2>
        <p class="lede">
            Thee Buhle Foundation is
            @(Registration.HasNpoNumber ? $"a registered non-profit organisation ({Registration.NpoDisplay})" : "a non-profit organisation")@(Registration.HasPboNumber ? $" and public benefit organisation ({Registration.PboDisplay})" : "")
            based at Cornwallis Street S.E.7, Vanderbijlpark, Gauteng. We are
            the responsible party for the personal information described below. Our information officer can be
            reached at <a href="mailto:hello@@theebuhlefoundation.co.za">hello@@theebuhlefoundation.co.za</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="d4" style="margin-top:40px">What we collect, and why</h2>

        <div class="tablewrap" style="margin-top:18px" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="What we collect and why">
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Who</th>
                        <th scope="col">What we hold</th>
                        <th scope="col">Why</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="row">Learners</th>
                        <td>Name, date of birth, grade, school, suburb, attendance record, school-issued marks, and a reference code.</td>
                        <td>To run the programmes, to report to parents, and to measure whether what we do works.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="row">Parents and guardians</th>
                        <td>Name, relationship, phone numbers, email address, and the consent decisions you record.</td>
                        <td>To contact you about your child, and to hold your permission for activities.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="row">Mentors and volunteers</th>
                        <td>Name, contact details, skills, availability, and clearance status. <b>Only the last four digits of your ID number.</b></td>
                        <td>To match you to a learner, and to record that you have been screened.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="row">Donors</th>
                        <td>Name, email address, phone number, amount, and the payment provider&rsquo;s reference. <b>No card details.</b></td>
                        <td>@(Registration.CanIssueCertificates ? "To issue your receipt and Section 18A certificate." : "To issue your receipt.")</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="row">Website visitors</th>
                        <td>The message you send us, and the IP address it came from.</td>
                        <td>To answer you, and to stop automated abuse of our forms.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <h2 class="d4" style="margin-top:40px">Things we deliberately do not do</h2>
        <ul style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8">
            <li>
                <b>We never store card details.</b> When you donate, your card is entered on our payment
                provider&rsquo;s own site. All that reaches us is your name, your email address and a payment
                reference.
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>We do not keep your full ID number.</b> It is needed for the SAPS clearance application,
                which we submit on your behalf. We retain only the last four digits, which is enough to match
                a returned certificate to an application.
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>We never publish a learner&rsquo;s name or photograph.</b> Learners appear publicly — on our
                Sponsor a Child page — as a reference code, a grade and a suburb. A sponsor is introduced to
                their learner by name only after the sponsorship is confirmed and the guardian has given
                written consent.
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>We do not sell, rent or share your information for marketing.</b> Ever, by anyone,
                for any amount.
            </li>
            <li>
                <b>We do not use advertising or analytics trackers on this website.</b> There are no
                third-party cookies, so there is no cookie banner to dismiss.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="d4" style="margin-top:40px">Consent, and changing your mind</h2>
        <p class="lede">
            Where we need your permission for something — a camp, a photograph, a trip — we ask for it
            explicitly and we keep the answer. <b>Withdrawing permission does not erase the record that you
            once gave it.</b> Instead, a withdrawal is recorded as a new decision, so the full history stays
            reconstructible: if you ask us what you agreed to and when you changed your mind, we can tell you
            precisely. That is a POPIA requirement and it is how our system is built.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
            You can withdraw a permission at any time in the parent app, or by phoning us on
            <a href="tel:+27710000000">+27 71 000 0000</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="d4" style="margin-top:40px">Your rights under POPIA</h2>
        <p class="lede">You have the right to:</p>
        <ul style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8">
            <li>ask what personal information we hold about you or your child, and receive a copy;</li>
            <li>ask us to correct anything that is wrong;</li>
            <li>ask us to delete information we no longer have a reason to keep;</li>
            <li>object to how we are using it;</li>
            <li>complain to the Information Regulator of South Africa.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="lede">
            Email <a href="mailto:hello@@theebuhlefoundation.co.za">hello@@theebuhlefoundation.co.za</a> and we
            will respond within 30 days. There is no charge for a first request.
        </p>

        <h2 class="d4" style="margin-top:40px">How long we keep things</h2>
        <ul style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8">
            <li><b>Learner records</b> — while the learner is on a programme, and then for five years, so we can confirm participation for a bursary or a job application later.</li>
            <li><b>Consent records</b> — seven years, as evidence of what was agreed.</li>
            <li><b>Donation records</b> — seven years, as SARS requires for Section 18A.</li>
            <li><b>Volunteer clearance documents</b> — seven years after the volunteer leaves, then purged automatically.</li>
            <li><b>Website enquiries</b> — two years.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="d4" style="margin-top:40px">How we protect it</h2>
        <p class="lede">
            Data is held in South Africa. Passwords are stored as Argon2id hashes and are never recoverable,
            including by us. Access is by role: a parent can see their own child and no other, and a
            safeguarding concern about a child is visible to our designated safeguarding lead alone. Every
            change to a learner&rsquo;s record is logged with who made it and when, and that log cannot be edited or
            deleted by anybody, including an administrator.
        </p>

        <h2 class="d4" style="margin-top:40px">Children</h2>
        <p class="lede">
            Most of the people we work with are under 18. We collect their information with the written
            consent of a parent or guardian, we hold the minimum we need to run a programme and report on it,
            and we never make it public. Learners over 13 with their own app account can see their own record
            and nobody else&rsquo;s.
        </p>

        <p class="dim" style="margin-top:40px;font-size:13px">
            Related: our <a href="/safeguarding">child safeguarding policy</a>, which sets out how a concern
            about a child is handled and who may work with our learners.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
